    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111323" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλόμουσ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>loving music</i> or
				<i>the Muses,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δελφῖνες</span> Arionl.<i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				14.61
			</span></i>: generally, <i>loving music and the arts, accomplished,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				259b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				548e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				5.1.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μουσικοὶ καὶ φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Mus.</u>
					p.62
				</span></i>
			 K., etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					358
				</span></i>
			 (anap.): <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ φ.,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλομουσία</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.984b
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
